To ensure proper propagation of labeled IPv6 prefixes with best-external route advertisement and label consistency, use the following BGP configuration:

```cli
configure router bgp
    advertise-external label-ipv6
```

This command specifically enables best-external advertisement for **labeled IPv6 unicast routes**, ensuring external paths are propagated even when the best overall route is internal. Label consistency is maintained as BGP-labeled unicast (RFC 8277) inherently preserves labels across the path when advertised via the `label-ipv6` address family. 

