To enable BGP-LS for topology propagation with OSPF integration on your Nokia 7750 SR routers, use this configuration sequence:

```cli
/configure router bgp
    family link-state
    link-state-import-enable
    group "BGP-LS-GROUP"
        family link-state
        neighbor <PEER_IP_ADDRESS>
            peer-as <REMOTE_AS_NUMBER>
        exit
    exit
exit
```

**Key details:**
1. `link-state-import-enable` globally activates IGP topology ingestion (including OSPF domains) into BGP-LS
2. The `family link-state` commands enable the link-state address family at both global and neighbor-group levels
3. Replace `<PEER_IP_ADDRESS>` and `<REMOTE_AS_NUMBER>` with your BGP-LS peer details

**Verification commands:**
```cli
show router bgp link-state database
show router bgp neighbor <PEER_IP_ADDRESS> advertised-routes link-state
``` 

This configuration propagates OSPF topology (nodes, links, prefixes) as BGP-LS TLVs to specified peers while maintaining compatibility with multi-vendor environments.
