   - `labeled-ipv6`: Handles labeled IPv6 unicast routes
   - `mvpn-ipv4`/`mvpn-ipv6`: Enables multicast VPN for IPv4/IPv6
   - `ipv4`: Maintains existing IPv4 peerings (assumes this is already configured)

2. **Add-Paths for Labeled IPv6**:
   - `label-ipv6 send 4 receive`: Negotiates send/receive of up to 4 paths per prefix (adjust `4` as needed)
   - Without this, add-paths remains disabled by default for labeled IPv6

3. **Non-Disruptive Deployment**:
   - Adding new address families refreshes sessions dynamically (no session reset)
   - Existing IPv4 peerings continue uninterrupted
   - Ensure peers support negotiated families (labeled IPv6/mVPN)

Replace `<peer-group-name>` with your BGP group. Validate peer compatibility with the new families before deployment.
