To set up BGP peering with the new regional AS using autonomous system 65001 on your Nokia 7750 SR, use the following CLI configuration commands. This ensures alignment with your existing routing policy and avoids disruption to current adjacencies:

```cli
configure router
    bgp
        group "NEW_REGIONAL" 
            peer-as <New_Regional_AS_Number> 
            local-as 65001 private no-prepend-global-as
            neighbor <New_Regional_Peer_IP>
                no shutdown
            exit
        exit
    exit
exit
```

### Key details:
1. **`group "NEW_REGIONAL"`**: Creates a dedicated BGP group for the new regional AS. Replace `"NEW_REGIONAL"` with your preferred group name.
2. **`peer-as <New_Regional_AS_Number>`**: Specifies the AS number of the new regional peer. Replace `<New_Regional_AS_Number>` with the peer's actual AS.
3. **`local-as 65001 private no-prepend-global-as`**:
   - Uses `65001` as the virtual AS for this peer group.
