    update-fault-tolerance
exit
```

### Key Details:
- Errors preventing NLRI parsing (e.g., critical length issues) will still reset sessions.
- Non-critical errors (e.g., minor length discrepancies) trigger `treat-as-withdraw` and log entries without session disruption.
- Default behavior (`no update-fault-tolerance`) resets sessions on errors; explicitly enabling this overrides the default.

Use the most granular level (neighbor > group > global) to limit scope. Logs are generated automatically; verify with your existing logging filters.
