To implement BGP graceful restart with a 10-minute recovery timer across your Nokia 7750 SR fleet, use the following CLI configuration commands. Replace `<group-name>` and `<neighbor-ip>` with your specific group and neighbor details:

```cli
/configure router bgp graceful-restart restart-time 600
/configure router bgp group "<group-name>" graceful-restart restart-time 600
/configure router bgp group "<group-name>" neighbor "<neighbor-ip>" graceful-restart restart-time 600
```

### Explanation:
1. **Global Configuration**:  
   Sets the restart timer to 600 seconds (10 minutes) for the entire BGP instance. This ensures all neighbors inherit this value unless overridden.
   ```cli
   /configure router bgp graceful-restart restart-time 600
   ```

2. **Group Configuration**:  
   Overrides the timer to 600 seconds for a specific BGP group. Apply this to every group to enforce consistency.
   ```cli
   /configure router bgp group "<group-name>" graceful-restart restart-time 600
   ```

3. **Neighbor Configuration**:  
   Explicitly sets the timer to 600 seconds for a specific neighbor (if individual overrides are needed). Use this if a neighbor has a unique configuration.
   ```cli
   /configure router bgp group "<group-name>" neighbor "<neighbor-ip>" graceful-restart restart-time 600
   ```

### Key Notes:
- **Scope**: Apply the global command universally. Repeat group-level commands for all BGP groups, and neighbor-level commands for any neighbors with custom settings.
- **Verification**: After configuration, advertise the new restart-time to neighbors by bouncing BGP sessions or using `clear router bgp` commands during the maintenance window.
- **Stability**: The 600-second timer ensures neighbors retain stale routes for up to 10 minutes during your router's restart, preventing route flapping.

> **Example for a group named "PEERS" and neighbor 192.0.2.1**:  
> ```cli
> /configure router bgp group "PEERS" graceful-restart restart-time 600
> /configure router bgp group "PEERS" neighbor 192.0.2.1 graceful-restart restart-time 600
> ```
