To prioritize SR tunnels from the backup OSPF instance for critical BGP prefixes while maintaining fallback to the primary IGP, use the following configuration:

```cli
/configure router policy-options
begin
prefix-list "critical-prefixes"
    prefix 192.0.2.0/24 exact
    prefix 203.0.113.0/24 exact
exit
policy-statement "set-backup-tag"
    entry 10
        from protocol ospf
        from route-type node-sid
        action accept
            tag set 100
        exit
    exit
exit
policy-statement "set-critical-tag"
    entry 10
        from prefix-list "critical-prefixes"
        action accept
            tunnel-tag set 100
        exit
    exit
    entry 20
        action accept
        exit
    exit
exit
commit
exit
/configure router ospf "backup"
    export "set-backup-tag"
exit
/configure router bgp
    import "set-critical-tag"
    next-hop-resolution
        labeled-routes
            resolution-filter
                lsp tag 100
                lsp
            exit
        exit
    exit
exit
```

**Explanation of key actions:**
1. Tag backup OSPF node-SID routes with `100` using an export policy
2. Match critical prefixes and set `tunnel-tag 100` via BGP import policy
3. Configure BGP next-hop resolution to:
   - First use LSPs with tag `100` (backup OSPF tunnels)
   - Fall back to any available LSP (primary IGP tunnels) if backup unavailable

**Operational notes:**
- Replace `critical-prefixes` with your actual critical networks
- Adjust OSPF instance name (`"backup"`) to match your environment
- Primary OSPF remains unmodified for default operation
- Tunnel resolution automatically fails over to primary when backup paths disappear
